e partial derivatives of $q$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂q}{∂x}=y,\\,\\frac{∂q}{∂y}=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂q}{∂x} & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂q}{∂y} & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂q}{∂\\theta } & =-(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =-{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0700e7b2-6f89-569b-80c9-76966b0a03ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} - \\frac{8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526158} {:answer/id #uuid "256ad1f0-227d-5ab3-8708-6eb324b90aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526169} {:answer/id #uuid "4bd87932-9556-54c2-bf44-b10dfc62190f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{- 3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526177} {:answer/id #uuid "570475a5-8df7-5112-9b0d-b5f4696e1d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} + \\frac{3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526178} {:answer/id #uuid "7c39e04f-c6b9-5a8b-8c78-12f97819a641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r \\left(\\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "256ad1f0-227d-5ab3-8708-6eb324b90aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526169} :answer-field/id #uuid "176d5247-bf57-548e-a7ea-4712f6f68f4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "16f3dbcc-22a8-51d5-90f3-bbe17bd367b9" :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y)=\\ln{\\left(4 x^{2} + 3 x y + y^{2} \\right)},$ find $\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $g(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta} & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\right)(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\right)(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $g$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x}=\\frac{8 x + 3 y}{4 x^{2} + 3 x y + y^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=\\frac{3 x + 2 y}{4 x^{2} + 3 x y + y^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{2 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂\\theta} & =\\left(\\frac{3 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\right)(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{2 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\right)(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} - \\frac{8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}})+(\\frac{2 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} + \\frac{3 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{- 3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 6 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17302592-36a5-57f1-a971-a