 :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $w(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r} & =\\frac{∂w}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂r}+\\frac{∂w}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂r} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{∂w}{∂x}\\right)(\\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{∂w}{∂y}\\right)(\\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $w$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x}=- 4 x - y,\\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y}=- x - 8 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =- 8 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂w}{∂r} & =(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(- 8 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})(\\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+(- 8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =- 8 r \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526224 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7623b2a1-2815-51c8-af36-c5449d7b4225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} - \\frac{8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526186} {:answer/id #uuid "a095650a-55e6-5374-a87f-11f9eca107d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526201} {:answer/id #uuid "b3de4b3d-f1b9-5b84-a580-865d3ba52584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} - \\frac{4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526206} {:answer/id #uuid "b997a104-b349-5dba-8d72-574ffb82c196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526209} {:answer/id #uuid "e06161ba-b711-53b6-a6be-89ac2b159b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{r \\left(3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a095650a-55e6-5374-a87f-11f9eca107d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526201} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf37e36c-be27-5f11-9b87-1e2003357f10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fad48590-44c0-5716-af2e-ae5d36de575e" :question/problem "Given that $h(x,y)=\\ln{\\left(4 x^{2} - 4 x y + 3 y^{2} \\right)},$ find $\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta},$ where $(x,y)$ are Cartesian coordinates and $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "Applying the multivariable chain rule for the function $h(x,y)$ with two independent variables $r$ and $\\theta,$ where $x=r\\cos\\theta$ and $y=r\\sin\\theta,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta} & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta}+\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\right)(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\right)(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $h$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x}=\\frac{8 x - 4 y}{4 x^{2} - 4 x y + 3 y^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂y}=\\frac{- 4 x + 6 y}{4 x^{2} - 4 x y + 3 y^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{- 4 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂\\theta} & =\\left(\\frac{- 4 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\right)(- r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)})+\\left(\\frac{6 r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\right)(r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} - \\frac{8 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}})+(\\frac{6 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}} - \\frac{4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 r^{2} \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 r^{2} \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 r^{2} \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{3 \\sin^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} - 4 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562595 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b0ce7d1-e3eb-5abe-aad3-5ec2e74afb0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 r (\\cos {4 \\theta} - 2) \\sin {\\theta} + 4 r \\sin {4 \\theta} \\cos {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562599} {:answer/id #uuid "4512ed8c-3ede-5a65-9f8f-a810c42e748e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 r^{2} \\sin {\\theta} \\sin {4 \\theta} - 2 r (\\cos {4 \\theta} - 2) \\cos {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562619} {:answer/id #uuid "5674929d-a824-55f0-8f30-82e8e0ca48d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 r \\sin {\\theta} \\sin {4 \\theta} - 2 r \\cos {\\theta} \\cos {4 \\theta} + 4 r \\cos {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562623} {:answer/id #uuid "801a07f3-db90-5408-b255-c06f0a469d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 r (\\cos {4 \\theta} - 2) \\cos {\\theta} + 4 r \\sin {\\theta} \\sin {4 \\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562638} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a57294-efde-52ac-930c-bfb39691209d" 