nd $(r,\\theta)$ are the corresponding plane polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will make use of the following chain rule formula:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=\\frac{∂u}{∂r}\\cos \\theta-\\frac{1}{r}\\frac{∂u}{∂\\theta}\\sin \\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $u$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂r}=9 r^{2} (\\cos {4 \\theta} - 2),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂\\theta}=- 12 r^{3} \\sin {4 \\theta}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =(9 r^{2} (\\cos {4 \\theta} - 2))\\cos \\theta-\\frac{1}{r}(- 12 r^{3} \\sin {4 \\theta})\\sin \\theta \\\\ & =-18{r}^{2}\\cos \\theta+9{r}^{2}\\cos 4\\theta\\cos \\theta+12{r}^{2}\\sin 4\\theta\\sin \\theta \\\\ & =3{r}^{2}(-6\\cos \\theta+3\\cos 4\\theta\\cos \\theta+4\\sin 4\\theta\\sin \\theta).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f840b5-46c8-591e-ac05-98c98fc28496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 r^{2} \\sin {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562612} {:answer/id #uuid "3826bc4e-b3a2-5171-b9c0-48a0a14a2bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 r^{2} \\cos {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562617} {:answer/id #uuid "727c8ffa-e135-5832-9124-74a049f2dbd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 r^{2} \\cos {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562631} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b912ba-04b8-5b75-bd8c-cdf14c09beea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 r^{2} \\cos {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562647} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6c602b-c6a2-58e9-a4e9-eeb4a1a3c560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 r^{3} \\cos {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186