}\\sin \\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $u$ with respect to $r$ and $\\theta:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂r}=- 9 r^{2} (\\sin {2 \\theta} - 3),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂\\theta}=- 6 r^{3} \\cos {2 \\theta}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =(- 9 r^{2} (\\sin {2 \\theta} - 3))\\cos \\theta-\\frac{1}{r}(- 6 r^{3} \\cos {2 \\theta})\\sin \\theta \\\\ & =27{r}^{2}\\cos \\theta-9{r}^{2}\\sin 2\\theta\\cos \\theta+6{r}^{2}\\cos 2\\theta\\sin \\theta \\\\ & =-3{r}^{2}(-9\\cos \\theta+3\\sin 2\\theta\\cos \\theta-2\\cos 2\\theta\\sin \\theta).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562653 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18656e36-b360-596c-906f-c6142433c6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 r \\sin {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562604} {:answer/id #uuid "246038ff-e08b-58fe-a4b1-bafce1919350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 r \\sin {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562608} {:answer/id #uuid "586adb3d-8dc3-5c10-b04c-05dd6518dacc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 r \\sin {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562624} {:answer/id #uuid "9c4350a9-7085-544f-bc6e-0361174ad019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 r \\cos {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562644} {:answer/id #uuid "e4493ba7-e108-5a71-9992-4b9775de69a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 r^{2} \\sin {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "586adb3d-8dc3-5c10-b04c-05dd6518dacc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 r \\sin {\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562624} :answer-field/